```ts
await within(dialog).findByLabelText(/Database service/);
```
But `within(dialog)` doesn't have `findByLabelText`? `within` returns queries including find*. Yes. Or use `await screen.findByLabelText(/Database service/)` (only one). Then click. Also wait for data load? After service auto-select, `listServiceDatabases`/`listServiceUsers` resolve; the "Use existing database" radio is always visible once services loaded, even while data loads. We can click it; then existing database select may show "No databases found" until data loads. We then `getByLabelText(/Existing database/)` which exists immediately; change to 'app' might fail if option not loaded. Wait for option text 'app' first. Use `await screen.findByRole('option', { name: 'app' })` inside dialog. Or wait for the select's options length.

Simpler: after opening dialog, wait for `Database service` select and then for `listServiceDatabases` to have been called. But data resolution microtask. Use:
```ts
const service = await within(dialog).findByLabelText(/Database service/);
await waitFor(() => expect((service as HTMLSelectElement).value).toBe('mysql'));
await fireEvent.click(within(dialog).getByLabelText('Use existing database'));
const dbSelect = within(dialog).getByLabelText(/Existing database/) as HTMLSelectElement;
await waitFor(() => expect(dbSelect.value).toBe('app'));
```
