Add a test for no active SQL service doesn't block site creation. This is a review focus. Test:
```ts
it('does not block site creation when no SQL service is active', async () => {
  mockApi.listServices.mockResolvedValue([]);
  await openOptionsStep();
  const toggle = screen.getByLabelText('Create or link a database') as HTMLButtonElement;
  await waitFor(() => expect(toggle.disabled).toBe(true));
  expect(screen.getByText(/no active SQL service/i)).toBeTruthy();
  expect(screen.getByRole('link', { name: 'Services' })).toBeTruthy();
  await fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Create site' }));
  await waitFor(() => expect(mockApi.createSite).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1));
  expect(mockApi.createSite).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.not.objectContaining({ database: expect.anything() }));
});
```
But the "Services" link text is inside a paragraph with "Install and activate ... from Services." `getByRole('link', {name:'Services'})` works. The notice only shows when enabled? In our template, when `!enabled` and services loaded empty, we show the empty hint, not the "No active SQL service" notice. Wait: `{:else if selectable.length === 0}` is inside the `enabled` branch. When disabled, the hint shows. The user doesn't see the notice. The spec says "If no active SQL service exists, the panel links to Services". We should show the notice even when disabled if no services. Our toggle is disabled and the hint says no DB will be linked, but no Services link. That's not compliant. Need to show the no-service notice when disabled and no selectable services. Restructure:
```svelte
{#if servicesError}
  Error
{:else if servicesLoaded && selectable.length === 0}
  <div class="notice">No active SQL service... <a>Services</a>...</div>
  {#if !enabled}<p class="empty-hint">No database will be linked...</p>{/if}
{:else if !enabled}
  <p class="empty-hint">...</p>
{:else if servicesLoading}
...
{:else}
...
```
But when loading, show hint. When loaded empty, show notice + hint. The toggle is disabled. Site creation proceeds. Good.

Let's restructure the template branches. Current:
```
{#if servicesError}
  Error
{:else if !enabled}
  hint
{:else if servicesLoading}
  loading
{:else if selectable.length === 0}
  notice
{:else}
  fields
{/if}
```
Change to:
```
{#if servicesError}
  Error
{:else if servicesLoaded && selectable.length === 0}
  <div class="notice">...</div>
  {#if !enabled}<p class="empty-hint">No database will be linked...</p>{/if}
{:else if !enabled}
  hint
{:else if servicesLoading}
  loading
{:else}
  fields
{/if}
```
But `servicesLoaded && selectable.length===0` is true while `servicesLoading` false. Good. If `servicesError`, error branch wins.
When `alwaysOn` and no services, `enabled` true, notice shows, no hint. Good.
When not alwaysOn and no services, toggle disabled, notice + hint. Good.

