Potential bug: When `alwaysOn` and available empty, `sync()` sets `value` with service_id '' (since enabled true). The dialog submit validation catches. Good.

Potential bug: When `alwaysOn` and services load with available, `selectService` is called. But `selectService` uses `databaseMode`/`userMode` current values. Good.

Potential bug: When Add Site panel is disabled, `loadServices` runs; if available length 0 and enabled false, `sync()` sets value null. Good.

Potential bug: `setEnabled(true)` when `servicesLoaded` and `selectable` has one service, calls `selectService`. Good.

Potential bug: `setEnabled(false)` calls `sync`, value null. Good.

Potential bug: `setEnabled(true)` when services loading and `selectable` empty: `sync` sets value with empty service. When load completes with available, `(alwaysOn || enabled) && !serviceID` -> selectService first. Good. If load completes with none, `enabled` false. Good.

Potential bug: `sync()` is called in `selectService` before data loads, with `databaseMode` maybe existing and `databaseName=''`; `request.database=''`, `user_id=''` (if existing). Validation catches. After data loads, sync updates. Good.

