Potential bug: Existing user `request.grant` omitted. Good.

Potential bug: For existing user with password typed, `request.password` included. For existing user with password blank, omitted. Good.

Potential bug: The password field is only shown if `!selectedUser.password_managed`. If the user is external but `password_managed` true (stored), no field. Good.

Potential bug: The password field's value persists when switching users? `setUserMode` clears password; changing user via select clears password. Good. Changing database doesn't clear password; okay.

Potential bug: `handleServiceChange` when id empty sets serviceID '', databases/users empty, sync. But `databaseName`/username remain; sync builds new_database with old name and service empty. Validation catches. Fine.

Potential bug: `loadServices` retry while enabled and serviceID set: `available.length>0`, `(alwaysOn||enabled) && !serviceID` false, `sync()` only; it doesn't reload databases/users. Fine.

Potential bug: `servicesLoaded` remains true after a failed retry? `servicesLoaded` true from first load; on retry error, servicesError set, servicesLoaded true. The template shows error. Good.

Potential bug: `onMount` always loads services even if `alwaysOn` false and panel disabled. This is intended to show availability. Good.

Potential bug: The Add Site panel uses `siteName={name}`. If the user changes the site name after enabling, the default database/username don't update because `sync` only on input. There's no effect to update defaults when siteName changes. The plan says "Default new database name to slugify(name) || 'app'; default new username to the same slug". At the time the panel is enabled, `name` is already slugified. If the user goes back to step 1 and changes the name, then returns to step 3, the DatabasePicker component may be destroyed and remounted (step 3 branch), so `onMount`/`setEnabled` uses the new name. The Add Site state `dbRequest` persists across step navigation, but the picker component remounts with `enabled` false (internal) and `value` bound to old dbRequest; it doesn't initialize `enabled` from value. This is a bug: if the user enables the DB panel, goes back to step 1, changes name, then returns to step 3, the DatabasePicker remounts with `enabled=false`, but `dbRequest` is still non-null. The review row still shows the DB selection, but the panel says "No database will be linked" and the toggle is off. If they click Create site, `validateAll` sees `dbRequest` non-null and may validate the old selection; the payload still includes it. Inconsistent UI.

We need to handle component remount with a non-null `value`: initialize `enabled = Boolean(value)` and populate internal state from `value`? Or parent should reset `dbRequest` when leaving step 3? Simpler: in `onMount`, if `value` is non-null, set `enabled = true` and hydrate internal fields from `value`. But the value doesn't include display metadata for existing user username; we can still set serviceID, modes, names, userID, password, grant. Then loadServices will auto-select and data. This makes remount consistent.

Alternatively, keep the DatabasePicker mounted outside the step branch? Not easy.

Let's implement hydration in `onMount`:
```ts
onMount(() => {
  if (value) {
    enabled = true;
    serviceID = value.service_id;
    databaseMode = value.new_database ? 'new' : 'existing';
    databaseName = value.new_database?.name ?? value.database ?? '';
    userMode = value.new_user ? 'new' : 'existing';
    username = value.new_user?.username ?? '';
    userID = value.user_id ?? '';
    password = value.password ?? '';
    grant = value.grant ?? value.new_user?.grants?.[0]?.preset ?? 'read_write_schema';
    summary = buildSummary();
  } else if (alwaysOn) {
    enabled = true;
    databaseName = defaultName();
    username = defaultName();
  }
  void loadServices();
});
```
But `buildSummary()` uses `selectedService` from `services` (empty on mount) and `selectedUser` from `users` (empty). It will set serviceName to serviceID, username for existing to '' until data loads. After `loadServices` auto-selects? `loadServices` sees `serviceID` set, `(alwaysOn||enabled) && !serviceID` false -> `sync()`; it doesn't load databases/users for the existing serviceID. We need to load service data on mount if serviceID set. In `loadServices`, after services loaded:
```ts
if (available.length === 0) ...
else if ((alwaysOn || enabled) && !serviceID) await selectService(available[0].id);
else if ((alwaysOn || enabled) && serviceID) await selectService(serviceID);
else sync();
```
But `selectService(serviceID)` resets databaseName/username to defaults, losing hydrated values. We need a `selectService(id, preserve = false)` or a separate `loadServiceData(id)` that doesn't reset. Refactor:
- `selectService(id)` resets and loads.
- `loadServiceData(id)` loads databases/users without resetting, then sets existing mode selections if empty and syncs.
In `loadServices`, if serviceID set and enabled, call `loadServiceData(serviceID)`.

But is this edge case worth the complexity? The plan says the wizard stays three steps and users can navigate back. It's a real UX bug. We should fix.

Simpler approach: Parent resets `dbRequest` and `dbSummary` when leaving step 3? That would discard the DB selection when going back, which is worse.

Another approach: Keep the DatabasePicker mounted across steps by moving it outside the `{#if step === 3}` block and hiding it with CSS? Not clean.

Hydration is the right fix. Let's implement.

Refactor `selectService`:
```ts
