  expect(screen.queryByRole('button', { name: /reset password/i })).toBeNull();
  expect(screen.getByText(/external password entry is not available in v1/i)).toBeTruthy();
});
```
Current code has Set password -> RED.
4. External user with stored password no reset:
```ts
it('does not offer reset for an external user with a stored password', async () => {
  mockDb.listSiteDatabases.mockResolvedValue({ links: [SITE_DB_LINK] });
  mockDb.listServiceUsers.mockResolvedValue({ users: [{ ...APP_USER, managed: false }] });
  await renderSite('blog');
  expect(await screen.findByRole('button', { name: /reveal password for app/i })).toBeTruthy();
  expect(screen.queryByRole('button', { name: /reset password/i })).toBeNull();
});
```
Current code no reset at all -> passes, but after implementation it ensures only managed. Good.

5. Fallback duplicate inference when linked_sites absent:
```ts
it('falls back to duplicate link inference when linked_sites is absent', async () => {
  mockDb.listSiteDatabases.mockResolvedValue({ links: [SITE_DB_LINK, { ...SITE_DB_LINK, id: 'lnk_2', database: 'blog' }] });
  mockDb.listServiceUsers.mockResolvedValue({ users: [{ ...APP_USER, linked_sites: undefined }] });
  await renderSite('blog');
  expect(await screen.findAllByText('shared user')).toHaveLength(2);
});
```
But two links with same user and different databases; card renders two rows. `findAllByText('shared user')` length 2. Current code uses duplicate inference already, so this test passes before implementation. It's a regression test for fallback. Good.

